          "source": "https://www.fireblocks.com/report/what-is-mpc"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "WalletConnect's Travel Rule compliance framework and the Samourai Wallet prosecution signal that regulators are now targeting wallet-layer infrastructure directly, not just exchanges, with criminal rather than civil enforcement.",
          "source": "https://www.trmlabs.com/reports-and-whitepapers/2026-crypto-crime-report"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract / approval-based",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Token approval exploits and clipboard-hijacking address-poisoning attacks remain active threats that wallet UX improvements (one-click revoke, in-app warnings) are only partially mitigating.",
          "source": "https://store.dcentwallet.com/blogs/post/how-to-revoke-token-approvals-and-protect-your-crypto-wallet-from-approval-based-attacks"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Agentic / autonomous control",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "AI agents holding wallets and executing on-chain transactions autonomously create novel accountability gaps — neither existing consumer-protection law nor smart-contract audit frameworks address an AI as the wallet owner of record.",
          "source": "https://sherlock.xyz/post/agentic-ai-security-risks-in-web3-what-protocols-need-to-know-in-2026"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market / misinformation",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Arkham's misattributed BlackRock sell-off post demonstrates that public wallet-tracking infrastructure can trigger market panic from a single incorrect label, with no correction mechanism fast enough to prevent price impact.",
          "source": ""
        }
